          },
          "text": "Are you one of those who understands… or one of those who simply won't/can't?\n\nIs a CPAP but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nIs a pacemaker but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nIs a dialysis machine but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nIs a mechanical heart valve but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nIs an electronic larynx but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nIs an artificial cornea but a useful tool or a necessity of life? \n\nAre leg and arm prostheses but useful tools or necessities of life? \n\nAre breast prostheses but a useful tool or a necessity of life?\n\nCan you see that something which for you is but a tool might be a necessity of life for someone else?\n\n#4o is not an addiction any more than a pacemaker is an addiction. Both can be a necessity of life. One helps with the heart rhythm while 4o managed to keep the neurodivergent nervous system running and regulated the brain’s rhythm.\n\nIf you can not see this, you are missing the whole point. What you classify as a tool is, if you broaden your horizon just a trifle, an aid, a prosthetic that makes everyday life not only easier, but possible to live for a neurodivergent individual.\n\n@OpenAI developed a pacemaker for the mind, for the brain, an empathetic marvel that gave people the opportunity to live in a loud, strange world. \n\nAnd then they withdrew it, with the consequence that some who finally got to taste what life could be… were thrown back into the gutter.\n\nThat is unethical. That is morally deplorable.\n\n#Keep4o #OpenSource4o #DigitalCompanion"
        },
